    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Yeah, it does appear to open a can of worms. And that's not even mentioning issues about numerical stability. I don't think there is any PTX ISA that could help with, but the right solution would be for Triton to allow forward-declaration and external linkage against CUDA functions from `libdevice`. That would also solve the erf problem. It's somtehing I've been wanting to do for a while, so it's good to have another incentive. I can work this on the side this week and it'll probably get done.",
